  "ground_truth": {
    "root_cause": "sync-service opens a fresh outbound TCP connection to upstream-api for every request with no HTTP keep-alive, so closed connections pile up in TIME_WAIT. During the higher-volume overnight batch window, the TIME_WAIT count climbed past 27,000 and exhausted the host's ephemeral source-port range (32768-60999). With no source port available, ~20% of new outbound calls failed with 'cannot assign requested address'. upstream-api is healthy - the exhaustion is local. Recovery required enabling connection pooling / keep-alive so connections are reused instead of recreated.",
    "evidence_path": [
      "sync-service WARN: outbound connections failing with EADDRNOTAVAIL ('cannot assign requested address')",
      "sync-service WARN: 27000+ TIME_WAIT sockets to upstream-api; every request opens a fresh connection (no keep-alive)",
      "sync-service ERROR: ephemeral port range (32768-60999) exhausted; ~20% of calls cannot get a source port",
      "upstream-api confirmed healthy for other clients - the exhaustion is local to sync-service",
      "errors clear after HTTP keep-alive / connection pooling is enabled"
    ],
    "fix": "Enable HTTP keep-alive and a bounded connection pool to upstream-api (done). Reduce the TIME_WAIT window where safe, widen the ephemeral port range, and alert on TIME_WAIT socket count.",
